vox}, {data, mask} or {data, mask, vox}.\\n\\nRegisterData[target, moving] \
registers the moving data to the target data. target can be 2D or 3D. moving \
can be the same of one dimension higher than the target.\\nThe inputs target \
and moving can be in the forms: data, {data, vox}, {data, mask} or {data, \
mask, vox}.\\n\\nOutput is the registered data with the dimensions of the \
moving data. \\nIf OutputTransformation is True it also outputs the \
translation, rotation scale and skew of all images or \
